<title> Nipple Discharge: Diagnosis.</title>
<graphic href="eee0239-w001.gif" />
<cell type="start" id="cell-1">
<label>Patient presents with nipple discharge. Likely to have medication as cause?</label>
<path target="cell-3">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-2">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-2">
<label>Bilateral discharge?</label>
<path target="cell-5">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-4">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-4">
<label>Unilateral, multiductal, nonbloody, no mass.</label>
<path target="cell-6">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-7">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-6">
<label>Mammogram (ultrasound if age &lt;30); likely duct ectasia; monitor if results are negative; consider referral if bothersome.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-7">
<label>Mass present?</label>
<path target="cell-8">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-9">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-8">
<label>Mammogram plus needle biopsy or referral; see chapter on breast lump.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-9">
<label>Single duct, bloody, clear or serous?</label>
<path target="cell-10">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-11">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-10">
<label>Ultrasound, mammogram if age &#x003E;30, referral for duct excision if BI-RADs 1-3, tissue biopsy if BI-RADS 4-5.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-11">
<label>Ultrasound, mammogram if age &#x003E;30; consider referral for ductography or ductoscopy, tissue biopsy if BI-RADS 4-5.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-5">
<label>Milky discharge?</label>
<path target="cell-13">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-12">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-12">
<label>Yellow-green or dark green and nonbloody discharge?</label>
<path target="cell-15">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-14">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-14">
<label>Serous or bloody discharge or mass present?</label>
<path target="cell-7">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-15">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-15">
<label>Likely ductal ectasia or fibrocystic breast; monitor, order mammogram if over age 40; consider mammogram if over age 30 or ultrasound if under age 30 years.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-13">
<label>Pregnant or recent pregnancy?</label>
<path target="cell-17">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-16">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-16">
<label>Check serum prolactin and TSH; consider a pituitary MRI if prolactin is high.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-17">
<label>Monitor; consider serum prolactin or TSH if persistent.</label>
</cell>
<cell type="decision" id="cell-3">
<label>Omit or change. Discharge resolves?</label>
<path target="cell-18">Yes</path>
<path target="cell-2">No</path>
</cell>
<cell type="action" id="cell-18">
<label>Done.</label>
</cell>
</algorithm>
